+code + chip id check as the battle history; `GET /ui/card-stats/get-card-stats/{accessCode}/{chipId}`; the response
+holds no card identifiers). No DB schema change; it reads the existing tables:
+
+| Section | Source |
+|---|---|
+| Win rate by mode: Total, Offline (solo + team), Class solo, Class team, Mix, Fes, Other | win/loss record (lifetime). Total is never shown below the sum of the modes; Other = online battles outside Class / Mix / Fes (private rooms...) |
+| Totals: damage, avg damage, kills, no-damage battles, EX burst damage, Class 10-win streaks; burst types | player statistics, burst-type statistics |
+| By mobile suit (sortable: name, cost, battles, wins, losses, win rate, avg damage, avg taken, kills, kills/battle, no-damage battles, EX burst damage, last played) | "All modes" = lifetime per-suit statistics (`MobileSuitPvPStatistic`); a single mode = counted from battle history (only battles with a stored history row; online ones from the online-results build on). Suit names / costs from `wwwroot/data/MobileSuits.json` |
+| Recent battles (30): date, mode, suit, result, damage dealt / taken, time | battle history |
+
+Deaths per suit are not stored by the game save (only kills), so there is no K/D column.
+Tests: `Tests/Server.Tests/CardStatsTests.cs` (9): owner-only access, empty card, offline + online split by mode and
+suit, other cards excluded, recent cap, legacy totals, no secrets in the response, mode keys, per-mode table rows.
+
 ## Known gaps / risks
 * CheckMatching / CancelMatching are not authenticated: anyone who knows a node id can cancel that entry.
   (`BindMatchNodesToSourceIp` limits Check/Cancel to the IP that entered, but is not a login.)
